  "stage": {
    "note": "Makoko's smoking deck (world:place-is-one-screen), behind its door on the channel (world:entering-is-a-cut): a wide plank deck at the walk's height, half open, the women's trade. Drum kilns with round wire trays of fish and thin smoke rising under the lean-to of rusty iron, baskets of small fish and a cooler, a woman washing fish in a big black pot, the striped tarp over the front, firewood stacked by sacks of sawdust, washing on a line, the racks with their board beside the deck and a work canoe tied at its end. The deck is stood lowered by its height, so its boards are where the character walks; at night the embers glow and one bulb hangs under the lean-to.",
